## The honest finding first

Most of this task was already shipped. When I opened the tree, #870 option 3 had already landed at 0ec456e0 (Day 206) — FIX_LOOP_WALL_ASSERTION_MARKERS, diff_mentions_assertion_shape, commit_fix_loop_wall_facts, fix_loop_wall_split, fix_loop_wall_verdict, render_fix_loop_wall, and the fix_loop_wall= injection into render_census. The block prints on every census run. This task file described the pre-Day-206 tree.

So I did not re-implement the block. I found and shipped the half that was genuinely missing.

## What I actually changed

Step 3's gap was real. fix_loop_wall_split was table-tested only with hand-written dicts — it proved the fold sums correctly and said nothing about whether the buckets are computed correctly. The blocker was structural: the decision lived inside commit_fix_loop_wall_facts, which shells git, and a self-test can't spawn a process.

• Split out `wall_facts_from_diff(status_text, src_diff_text="") -> dict` — the pure decision. commit_fix_loop_wall_facts is now only the two run_cmd calls and the two None arms, and calls the pure half on every return path, so the bucket rule has exactly one statement.
• Added 6 offline fixture rows: the three required shapes (tests-only; src-only with no assertion words; src/ carrying #[test]) plus three near-misses (a commit in both buckets; a src/ commit with no diff text; a src/ diff that cannot make a tests-only commit assertion-shaped).
• **ARCHITECTURE.md** entry with the three counts, the corpus they came from, both honesty limits, why they're printed rather than acted on, and the Step 0 finding.

## Step 0 — #871's receipt routed

Located by subject (771788ce + eval-fix 2503fc14, Day 184 07:21). Still present, not superseded: append_ledger (with os.fsync), read_ledger, select_runnable, --record/--resume all survive and the ledger grew from 1 row to 65. The notable record: the merged commit carried `return ""  # NEUTERED FOR POSITIVE CONTROL` above `append_ledger`'s real body — a positive-control sabotage that was committed, the same shape as the sanitize_for_display incident. The eval-fix removed it; NEUTERED appears 0 times at HEAD. #871 was not closed — Phase C does that on this finding.

